# Scientific integrity and safety

- Refer to `docs/standards/scientific-integrity.md`.
- Scalp EEG is not a voxel-wise view of brain activity. Source-localized cortex maps are model-derived, resolution-limited and depend on electrode geometry, reference, conductivity assumptions, inverse regularization and artifacts.
- Display observed sensor features and model estimates distinctly. Show quality/confidence, smoothing, derivation method and calibration version.
- An anatomical MRI does not record live brain activity; a 3D external head scan is a different asset for physical headset fit.
- Validate ML by separate recording sessions; flag distribution shifts, missing channels and unsound claims of emotion/thought decoding.
- Do not provide clinical diagnosis or actionable treatment recommendations from prototype measurements.
